      "side": 1,
      "message": "`fFPCoordsMap` contains a list of the FPs which passed through `collectTransforms`/`liftTransforms`. \n\nConsider the case of an `fp` which did not exist in the `fFPCoordsMap` and also doesn\u0027t use sample coords. This processor would reach the bottommost `else` block. At this point we would do `fFPCoordsMap[\u0026fp].coordsVarying`, which would synthesize a new empty entry in the map (not the intent) and the following switch is doomed to fail.\n\nPreviously, `writeFPFunction` was only called by `emitRootFragProc` and it was safe to assume that `fFPCoordsMap` contained the passed-in `fp`, so this case wouldn\u0027t occur in practice.\n\nThis is no longer a safe assumption since we are calling `writeFPFunction` from the MeshGP now as well, and its `fp`s didn\u0027t participate in transform-lifting.\n\nSorry if this explanation is complex--I ended up rewriting it a few times since there are a lot of moving pieces.",
